//! flags: -p ssa

// The simplifier's common subexpressions key a block argument by its
// definition rather than its name (SSA/Simplify.cpp, key_value). What to
// read for: after promotion `dead` is an argument of the loop's header and
// of the merge block after `if i == limit { dead = true }`, and the two
// `not(dead)` -- the header's, on the value carried round the loop, and the
// body's, on the value the merge block just made -- are TWO instructions,
// the body's dispatching on its own. Keyed by the name alone the body's
// was the header's (2026-10-07, apps/pbrt: a killed path in the layered
// BxDF's walk went on scattering).

func [[export]] walk(n : i32, limit : i32) -> i32 {
    dead : mut bool = false;
    i : mut i32 = 0;
    kept : mut i32 = 0;
    while !dead && (i < n) {
        if i == limit {
            dead = true;
        }
        if !dead {
            kept = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    return kept;
}
